event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":80,"item_id":"rs_0c30853fdc2e871b016ac95306c54087d185869fd0b9d7b34c","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Evaluating port allocation for testing**\n\nI'm pondering whether I need to direct tests to spawn on port 0. It looks like I should specify an ephemeral port using net ephemeral, then close any negligible race conditions. I'm also considering whether to use stdout for listening or if health polling on a fixed ephemeral port might be better. I want to ensure the test is robust, with a child exit listener to stop properly, too."}

